From 39baa1852c60ba3af6269ac58888cc1777132571 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:56:34 +0000
Subject: ipa: softisp: Focus with the sensor's phase detection

Sensors that send their PD pixels as a metadata stream beside the image
need the host to compute the phase. Give the soft IPA the buffers of such
a stream: mapPdafBuffers() shares them once, processPdaf() measures one
with libipa's PdafPhase, on the layout the camera sensor helper provides,
and pdafProcessed() hands it back. The result, a phase and confidence
per region, is kept in the active state for the algorithms.

The Af algorithm reads the module's calibration from a "pdaf" block in
its tuning: shading gain maps per pupil side, applied before the phase is
measured, and a defocus conversion map, whose grid the phase is measured
on so that each region has its own coefficient. SoftwareIsp forwards the
calls, identifying buffers by cookie.

Contrast AF has to search: it cannot tell from one frame how far focus is
or in which direction, and a sharpness drop from motion looks like
defocus. Phase detection tells both, from a single frame. Use it when the
sensor has a PD stream and the tuning a defocus conversion map.

The defocus is the confidence-weighted mean over the central regions of
each region's phase in image pixels, plus the calibration's offset, times
its coefficient, in actuator codes. From Idle, a defocus beyond 7% of the
code range seen for three readings with the scene still, or any at first
focus, moves the lens straight to where the phase puts focus (through the
inverse of the focus map), and so does one during a contrast search. The
jump repeats until the defocus is within 2% of the range, at most three
times, then a fine contrast probe finishes; a phase that turns unreliable
falls back to a contrast scan, and focus beyond the end of travel goes to
the probe at once. Contrast AF runs unchanged whenever no central region
is confident.

The tuning's pdaf block gains an offset, in image pixels as the vendor
calibration gives it, and minConfidence (0.5 by default).

Once the phase puts the lens within 2% of the code range of focus, hold
focus there instead of finishing with a contrast probe: the phase is
accurate enough, and the probe only made the lens breathe. The same goes
for focus beyond the end of travel and for the jump limit. While the
phase confirms focus in Idle, contrast does not arm a refocus on a
sharpness drop either, as that is motion or exposure, not defocus.
Contrast AF still searches whenever the phase is not confident.

The Af algorithm now names the regions it uses, the central window, and
the IPA measures only those.

Without a defocus conversion map in the tuning, the Af algorithm cannot
use the phase, so decline the PD buffers and let the pipeline leave the
stream off. Log how long each measurement takes, at debug level.

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
